# Terminology

How this project designs its gates and its reference entries, and the measured reasons behind
each promotion or rejection. The stores themselves are `{{ project_prefix }}glossary/approved.yaml`
(hard gates), `{{ project_prefix }}glossary/reference.yaml` (binding, not gated; `kind` groups such
as proper names and one-word-two-senses) and `{{ project_prefix }}glossary/candidates.yaml`
(promotion decisions). The matching rules are in `docs/LITTRANS.md`.

## Gate design rules

What makes a `source` safe to gate here (discriminative, actually occurring in the source
text, correct orthography, nesting checked in both languages).

## Per-chapter promotion procedure

How candidates are measured before promotion (`tools/lt.cmd glossary check {{ project_rel }}`,
`glossary lookup --pages`), and when a chapter's terms are frozen.

## Measured rejections

Terms considered and not promoted, with the count or example that decided it.
